# SIP Extension Methods

## 1. INFO
- Sends mid-dialog control signals without changing media.
- Example: DTMF keypresses in IVR.

## 2. PRACK
- Acknowledges provisional 1xx responses reliably (RFC 3262).
- Ensures important early media info isn't lost.

## 3. SUBSCRIBE & NOTIFY
- SUBSCRIBE: Request to track an event/status.
- NOTIFY: Server pushes updates when status changes.

## 4. UPDATE
- Lightweight mid-call SDP update without re-INVITE.
- Works even before call is fully established.

## 5. MESSAGE
- Sends instant text messages (RFC 3428).
- No call/session needed.

## 6. REFER
- Commands recipient to contact a third party (RFC 3515).
- Used for call transfer.

## 7. PUBLISH
- Publishes user's presence state to server (RFC 3903).
- Example: Available, Busy, DND.

## Quick Cheat Sheet

| Method | Role | Analogy |
|--------|------|---------|
| INFO | Mid-call signaling | DTMF keypad |
| PRACK | Reliable 1xx delivery | Confirm provisional response |
| SUBSCRIBE/NOTIFY | Status tracking | Voicemail alert |
| UPDATE | Quick SDP update | Early codec change |
| MESSAGE | Instant messaging | SMS/Chat |
| REFER | Call transfer | Forward call |
| PUBLISH | Presence publication | Status update |
